Z||000004||loafer87gt||07-11-2000||01:36 AM||||I'm kinda dissapointed in the HP and torque numbers of a built up V6. I checked out Norris Racing Technology and for their full blown 3.4 its only putting down 169 HP at the wheels. To quote their site: <P>Bored & honed .030 oversize using torque plates.<BR>Align honed<BR>Decked for minimum quench area<BR>Special cam bearings installed<BR>Increased compression ratio<BR>Rings file fitted<BR>Rods resized using ARP bolts<BR>Camshaft degreed in<BR>Add to that our top of the line head & cam package, intake porting, and expert assembly. Price $3595 US<P>I know if I were putting 3600 bucks into building up an engine I would expect a hell of a lot more power than that from it! It seems like the cheapest way to get HP is to used some kind of forced injection system.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pretender||07-11-2000||05:34 PM||||that is alot of money for what you get a whole 50 real wheel hp. for that price you could install a quad 4 or even a 3.8 supercharged granted you could find one at the right price.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Shaun41178||07-11-2000||08:24 PM||||I know John Norris as his shop is about an hour from me and I have stopped in there  a few times.  He is also on a camaro message board that I post at. <P>You don't have all the info of that 3.4 that made 169 hp at the wheels.  For one thing, only the heads of that engine were touched.  Nothing else.  Only the heads were taken off and ported and such.  Also this 3.4 was in a camaro which is only rated at 160 hp at the flywheel to begin with which is about 120-130 or so at the wheels.  So just buy giving the heads a good port job and valve bowl cleanup and such they picked up 50 hp at the wheels plus a buttload of torque.  Can you imagine going from 140 hp in a fiero to 190 with the same port job?  Big difference yes and that is with no other mods<P>Also this camaro was dynoed at 169 but not tuned.  All the extra airflow into the engine needs more fuel.  The camaro that was tested needs a custom tuned prom.  The guy might have one by now as he said a company was making one for him.  So a chip with enhanced spark and fuel curves could get him another 10 hp or so as the stock camaro prom isn't too aggressive to begin with.<P>That 169 at the wheels was also with the stock cam.  Put a bigger cam in and much more power can be made. Headers and cat-back would work well too to make more power<P>So with just the heads being ported and such, I forget how much it costs for the heads with a full port job and new valves ana all that but I think I remember it saying in the neighborhood of $1k or so.<P>A bit expensive yes but with good head work a ton more power can be made with our little engines.  The power from an engine comes from the heads/top end.  Durability comes from the bottom end.<P>If I had an exra $1k to spend I would have that mod done to my heads for my 3.2.  I think with a port job like that and 5 angle valve job a 3.2 can see like 240 hp or so easy.  Another option out there for our little V6's.  At least someone is doing it.  I am glad about that.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||07-11-2000||10:42 PM||||Whoa.... 50hp at the WHEELS with just head work?  I find that very difficult to believe.  If anything, he would gain some hp and LOST a bit of torque unless he has other mods to take advantage of the extra flow.||||reg||1
